The dynamical mass is estimated as $$\begin{equation}
 M_{\rm dyn} = \frac{5 R_e \sigma^2}{G}
\end{equation}$$ where $G$ is the gravitational constant, $R_e$ is the effective radius, and $\sigma$ is the velocity dispersion of the gas, in this case from the \[C I\] line, $\sigma_{\rm gas} = 34^{+16}_{-9}$ km s$^{-1}$.

